hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1240","Salam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, H, and Ali bin Hajr Al-Saadi told us, Jarir, H, narrated to us Yusuf bin Musa, narrated by Jarir, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray While he was sitting after he had entered the age, when thirty or forty verses remained of the surah, he stood up and recited them, then bowed, except that Ali, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not recite any of the night prayers while sitting, until he entered the age.”"
"1241","Bundar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Khams narrated to us, H. Ya’qub bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Ulayya narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, both of them On the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: I said to Aisha, “Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray sitting?” She said: “After people destroyed him.” Al-Dawrqi said: She said: Yes, after the people destroyed it."
